.DS_Store

# distribution bundles (built on demand, never committed)
/dist/

# generated indexes — this plugin's own output is never committed by the plugin,
# and shouldn't be committed here by accident either
/workspace-index.md
/*.index.md

# build-tool caches — an IDE or Java language server ran Gradle inside a test fixture once
# (tests/fixtures/classify/gradle-groovy/.gradle/, 2026-10). Fixtures must stay byte-exact.
.gradle/

# ── PUBLISH-TIME EXCLUSION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL-ONLY: the whole docs tree and CLAUDE.local.md. Everything else ships — including the
# root CLAUDE.md, which holds contributor conventions only (touchstone's pattern, 2026-10-14).
#   * docs/superpowers/ — historical specs/plans; carry origin-workspace detail.
#   * docs/findings/ and CLAUDE.local.md — internal project memory: status, history, evidence.
# tests/run-all.sh's "shipped files don't cite local docs" gate keeps every SHIPPED file from
# pointing at these, and computes what ships from THIS file.
#
# ⚠️ THESE RULES DO NOTHING TO THE CURRENT REPO. These files are already TRACKED here, and
# .gitignore never untracks anything. The exclusion becomes real only at the fresh `git init`
# planned for publish. Pushing THIS repo to a remote would publish them regardless.
#
# Verify after the fresh init, before the first push:
#   git ls-files | grep -E '^(docs/|CLAUDE\.local\.md$)'   # must print NOTHING
/docs/
/CLAUDE.local.md
